<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:25Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Zelensky says Ukraine ready to de-escalate if Russia halts strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5764b1d5fd94d6e360f5e36cf34e2e94598f214df063171c4ba5e5be9c349b50</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:04:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T22:57:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-zelensky-says-ukraine-ready-to-de-escalate-if-russia-halts-strikes--596ec22eafa5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-zelensky-says-ukraine-ready-to-de-escalate-if-russia-halts-strikes" /><summary type="html">Ukraine is ready to halt attacks on Russian energy infrastructure if Moscow does the same, President Volodymyr Zelensky said Monday, after US President Donald Trump announced an apparent agreement between the two sides. Kyiv also warned that intensifying Russian strikes on Ukraine’s rail network are worsening each week.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'The very existence of LGBTQI people is seen as obscene', Turkish activist says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f17fb9ddd7df5ee6531876e7fa7264d969aa0c2d11ebad2e1c24f8ed51401176</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:02:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260914-the-very-existence-of-lgbtqi-people-is-seen-as-obscene-turkish-activist-says--7e48c4e3384e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260914-the-very-existence-of-lgbtqi-people-is-seen-as-obscene-turkish-activist-says" /><summary type="html">Turkish police on Sunday swooped on gay bars and the homes of LGBTQ activists, arresting at least 60 people in raids authorities said were aimed at boosting traditional family values, officials and activists said. Turkey's LGBTQ community has frequently been targeted by the government, with President Recep Tayyip Erdogan lashing it as a "deviant movement" of "perverts" responsible for the falling birth rate. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with Yildiz Tar, Editor-in-Chief of KaosGL.org.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Leaders urge EU to boost Arctic role to tackle Russia 'threat'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba26dd048363b8479899fe290cc5abd872e84f8b74d1ae5e5c5a6d2d5decc41a</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:06:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/leaders-urge-eu-to-boost-arctic-role-to-tackle-russia-threat--d1df20e91748.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/leaders-urge-eu-to-boost-arctic-role-to-tackle-russia-threat" /><summary type="html">Twelve European countries meeting in Finland on Monday urged the European Union to beef up its presence in the Arctic, a geopolitical battleground caught between Russia and US President Donald Trump. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Leaders urge EU to expand Arctic presence amid Russia 'threat'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5afc1642ecfffccaaa4e920f5622c47ac3fbcaf905e84d70793cd472c3b93fdf</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T17:41:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-leaders-urge-eu-to-expand-arctic-presence-amid-russia-threat--e35c64118e5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-leaders-urge-eu-to-expand-arctic-presence-amid-russia-threat" /><summary type="html">Twelve European countries on Monday called for the European Union to step up its presence in the Arctic, as melting ice opens new maritime routes while growing tensions with Russia and the United States increasingly put the region in the geopolitical spotlight.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden faces political uncertainty after knife-edge election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3613730e95e00ca91af00575b5d0c455ecbe09e529bdf58261478d0228d63863</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T09:25:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-sweden-faces-political-uncertainty-after-knife-edge-election--1048b951361e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-sweden-faces-political-uncertainty-after-knife-edge-election" /><summary type="html">Sweden was bracing for a protracted struggle to form a government on Monday after election results showed a thin and uncertain lead for the left-wing opposition, while the far-right Sweden Democrats lost ground for the first time since entering parliament 16 years ago.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden Election Aftermath: A hard night for the hard right?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b2f0415ae52a5258533acb3af55b8ff6b2a9fe8dc57d76ea14f13e44d39b801</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T19:04:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-sweden-election-aftermath-a-hard-night-for-the-hard-right--3a3a6902f6a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-sweden-election-aftermath-a-hard-night-for-the-hard-right" /><summary type="html">FRANCE 24’s Gavin Lee speaks to Scandinavia Correspondent Trine Villeman for some analysis on how Sweden has voted in the 2026 election.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden's centre-left holds razor-thin edge as exit polls show tight race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25db4af1300da725dff5a2ff32fd7cb5723fa18efde748b4d6ad875e89c14539</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T18:25:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-sweden-s-centre-left-opposition-leads-election-as-far-right-slips-exit-polls-show--f5ea96e6c759.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-sweden-s-centre-left-opposition-leads-election-as-far-right-slips-exit-polls-show" /><summary type="html">Sweden's general election remained too close to call early Monday, with nearly 90 percent of votes counted. Four opposition parties led by Social Democrat Magdalena Andersson held a one-seat parliamentary lead over Prime Minister Ulf Kristersson's right-wing bloc, which includes the Sweden Democrats, as both leaders said they were ready to govern.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, Poland condemn Russia after drone strikes train near border</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f462b421ad317f8ed8370f1264007661d0e95f70d1067ec684ace95449526670</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T17:59:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-poland-ukraine-slam-russian-strikes-near-border-as-escalation--312f03179fa8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-poland-ukraine-slam-russian-strikes-near-border-as-escalation" /><summary type="html">Ukraine and Poland on Sunday condemned Russian strikes close to the Polish border as an "escalation" in the war, after drones struck a Warsaw-bound train. Ukraine's rail operator said former British PM Boris Johnson and ex-US CIA director David Petraeus were at a border train station nearby around the time the train was hit.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden: Tight election puts all eyes on the far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92e3de1413ccdbb174280df0953675c11385eb1131e7e4f56b89d829f61f4ef4</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T15:55:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sweden-tight-election-puts-all-eyes-on-the-far-right--e820006209b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sweden-tight-election-puts-all-eyes-on-the-far-right" /><summary type="html">Swedes are voting in a closely fought general election that could see the far-right Sweden Democrats enter government for the first time. With immigration, crime and the economy dominating the campaign, Prime Minister Ulf Kristersson and Social Democrat leader Magdalena Andersson are locked in a neck-and-neck race.</summary></entry><entry><title>Swedish far-right eyes role in government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:316a41b34137d7dde0d62372894120244cd8f925004cac21dffa02e5f32c7008</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:11:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/swedish-far-right-eyes-role-in-government--89cf8fdd015f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/swedish-far-right-eyes-role-in-government" /><summary type="html">As Sweden heads into a closely fought election, the far right is gaining ground by tapping into concerns over crime and security, issues that some voters increasingly associate with migration. On FRANCE 24, Stockholm University sociologist Zeth Isaksson said the movement has also softened its image in recent years, making it more acceptable to a broader electorate, while also cautioning against overstating the strength of the far right in Sweden.</summary></entry><entry><title>Sweden election: A turning point for the far right?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d5800361730b344769004d4e18464943a412d344a19698b9ea75433fb2b4635</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:48:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sweden-election-a-turning-point-for-the-far-right--20fbe48330d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sweden-election-a-turning-point-for-the-far-right" /><summary type="html">The stakes are high in Sweden's general election, with the far right poised to enter government for the first time. TV4 News journalist Markus Karlsson-Bourrioux explains how opinion polls shifted from a comfortable centre-left lead to a tight race over the summer, and how far-right ideas have gained ground since the last election in 2022.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany: Thousands rally against far-right after AfD victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46d50cd0ff3b5986844deedfd8b76197d3c418b2cec7be6c717a4bc67fe97399</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:41:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/germany-thousands-rally-against-far-right-after-afd-victory--38396b69fe17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/germany-thousands-rally-against-far-right-after-afd-victory" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of people marched in around 20 cities across Germany to protest the rise of the far right after the AfD's historic victory in the Saxony-Anhalt state election. Demonstrators said they were defending democracy as mainstream parties continue to rule out governing with the AfD.</summary></entry><entry><title>Swedes vote in close general election that could usher far right into government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d63dc1e67cb8566732ad0cf4c40c2fff847ff501c2d723f466dcd3ea57ff2717</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T06:16:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-swedes-vote-in-close-general-election-that-could-usher-far-right-into-government--c14a0b3c76df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-swedes-vote-in-close-general-election-that-could-usher-far-right-into-government" /><summary type="html">Swedes are heading to the polls Sunday for a general election that will either bring a far right party into government for the first time or shift the country back towards the liberalism it has long been known for. The centre-left opposition holds a narrow lead over the ruling right-wing bloc but Prime ⁠Minister Ulf Kristersson's four-party alliance – which includes the far right Sweden Democrats – has been catching up in the final weeks of campaigning.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands protest against far-right AfD party in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4679fcf0b91d088ad2fd4059a65232cb0de84ca9554817ec68c64a47feeb329</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T17:12:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-tens-of-thousands-of-people-protest-in-germany-against-far-right-afd--3bb68df54c54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-tens-of-thousands-of-people-protest-in-germany-against-far-right-afd" /><summary type="html">About 150,000 demonstrators took to the streets in around 20 cities across Germany on Saturday against the far-right AfD, after the party scored a crushing victory in a state election last week. The Alternative for Germany (AfD) topped the vote in the eastern region of Saxony-Anhalt, and is now seeking to form the first extreme-right state government in Germany since World War II.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Kremlin says meeting between Putin and Zelensky at Miami G20 'impossible'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1856e206fbcf10ebe1fb82aa21abc46da42d4ba30712a8642781773d307caccf</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T09:27:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-zelensky-willing-to-meet-putin-at-g20-kremlin-still-to-confirm-attendance--a496a636c055.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-zelensky-willing-to-meet-putin-at-g20-kremlin-still-to-confirm-attendance" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said he was willing to meet Russian leader Vladimir Putin at the G20 summit in Miami for talks on ending the war. However, the Kremlin immediately ruled it out, saying it was "impossible" and that a meeting would only take place in Russian capital Moscow.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French police suspect Normandy train derailment was result of sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:969ba2d71909c1e687c3e9abf8d573a6493783b1892107ca6645f4813f9517f0</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T08:48:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-french-police-investigate-suspected-sabotage-in-train-derailment--ddcadeb5d26c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-french-police-investigate-suspected-sabotage-in-train-derailment" /><summary type="html">A police source said Saturday that French investigators suspect sabotage caused a train derailment in northwest France after a fragment of rail was found on the track. At least 44 people were injured in the derailment that occurred a day earlier, including an 18-year-old woman "in a critical condition".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says unified Ireland ‘would be fantastic' during Dublin trip</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd97d7c8f9fd778b257305ff87b350f04a2c6f25d172eabd55fbe401ad4ca08f</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T07:51:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-trump-arrives-in-dublin-for-talks-with-ireland-s-leaders-before-attending-golf-tournament--fbbff38c8ec1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-trump-arrives-in-dublin-for-talks-with-ireland-s-leaders-before-attending-golf-tournament" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Saturday said a unified Ireland would be “fantastic" during a weekend visit to a major tournament at his Irish golf course. The two-day trip to Ireland is the latest example of how the US leader blends his official duties with his personal interests.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Céline Dion poised for emotional comeback concert in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae3dd029cde0b8db40babbbb83e500c119d9bb226646fb3fbf5620812f67cd06</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T05:23:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-a-legend-celine-dion-poised-for-emotional-comeback-in-paris--d2f545b260c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-a-legend-celine-dion-poised-for-emotional-comeback-in-paris" /><summary type="html">Céline Dion is set to return to the stage in Paris on Saturday for her first full concert in six years, capping a years-long battle with a rare autoimmune disorder and marking a major milestone in the Canadian superstar’s comeback.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Battle over 'pervert' AI glasses in Europe's line of sight after scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f408c0b76076ce88f15dca78f8000300d3d6cedcf15a4405343ff4e99492f981</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T05:15:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-battle-over-pervert-ai-glasses-in-europe-s-line-of-sight-after-scandal--5b6fbdddc4a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-battle-over-pervert-ai-glasses-in-europe-s-line-of-sight-after-scandal" /><summary type="html">A scandal involving girls and women filmed secretly by "pervert"  AI glasses has sparked growing concern over this emerging technology – with a petition in Britain demanding a ban on their sale. Anyone wearing smart glasses can take photos, film videos or interact with an AI assistant, with sales now hitting the millions.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky urges Trump to impose new Russia sanctions 'now', after deadly Ukraine strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b730cafe46122649c3434b6306e428a00d1232403cbc642267625414c6334548</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T19:13:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-zelensky-urges-trump-to-impose-new-russia-sanctions-now-after-deadly-ukraine-strikes--228fa885e3a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-zelensky-urges-trump-to-impose-new-russia-sanctions-now-after-deadly-ukraine-strikes" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on Friday urged US President Donald Trump to impose new sanctions on Russia over deadly strikes on Ukraine, as Kyiv and Moscow step up attacks and US-led efforts to end the war remain deadlocked.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Elections in Russia: the 1001 tricks to remove inconvenient candidates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be59a7e4589f25b7968f47a5e761078ffd385c9973dd160002f0aae43bdbb542</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T16:11:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-elections-in-russia-the-1001-tricks-to-remove-inconvenient-candidates--c49abd54b7c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-elections-in-russia-the-1001-tricks-to-remove-inconvenient-candidates" /><summary type="html">The Russian authorities are using dubious claims to disqualify candidates previously cleared to run in the parliamentary election from September 18 to 20. The war in Ukraine is making the Kremlin even more cautious about who is allowed to campaign.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>I'm extremely worried by extremists that win elections in Europe: Luxembourg's PM Luc Frieden</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:879b824464caac2d3900cc5373773baf1a7e7baee552c8e65435417a548649e7</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:53:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260911-i-m-extremely-worried-by-extremists-that-win-elections-in-europe-luxembourg-s-pm-luc-friede--96d71fcdb103.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260911-i-m-extremely-worried-by-extremists-that-win-elections-in-europe-luxembourg-s-pm-luc-frieden" /><summary type="html">"European strategic autonomy" is a buzz phrase in Brussels and in EU capitals these days. What does it mean for space policy? That was one of the central points that we raised with the Prime Minister of Luxembourg, Luc Frieden, during his visit to Paris for the International Space Summit hosted by the French government on September 9 and 10. Major American aerospace companies were noticeably absent from the summit while the feud between Brussels and the Trump administration continues.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>A fire destroys part of a migrant camp in the Spanish enclave of Ceuta</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f0ffb094e47d6cabca8612ae9af4d416cf7549446bc1df684e2e2203b8159d6</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:41:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-a-fire-destroys-part-of-a-migrant-camp-in-the-spanish-enclave-of-ceuta--b8e12cf63ee7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-a-fire-destroys-part-of-a-migrant-camp-in-the-spanish-enclave-of-ceuta" /><summary type="html">An apparently accidental fire destroyed about 40 shacks at a migrant camp in Ceuta, local media reported, but caused no injuries, Spanish police told AFP on Friday. The North African enclave saw tens of thousands of migrants arrive from Morocco in late July.</summary></entry><entry><title>French far-right leader polling ahead for 2027 election: should the EU be afraid?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:723607d74ec9812085fcdf3e8e5d00801ad56b27b0a000142410c09967676dcb</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:14:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-far-right-leader-polling-ahead-for-2027-election-should-the-eu-be-afraid--714a1da24d6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-far-right-leader-polling-ahead-for-2027-election-should-the-eu-be-afraid" /><summary type="html">In Brussels, opinion polls coming out of France have not escaped attention. Two polls see far right leader Marine Le Pen beating all her likely rivals in the French presidential election, which is set to take place in April and May of next year.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Did the War on Terror succeed? Or did Washington fall into al Qaeda’s trap?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ea64f77f1d540da5df65fa19c5d9a2e5a4de2c18d3d0e9eb1fea8df2e8af638</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:16:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260911-did-the-war-on-terror-succeed-or-did-washington-fall-into-al-qaeda-s-trap--52617987fc7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260911-did-the-war-on-terror-succeed-or-did-washington-fall-into-al-qaeda-s-trap" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW: Friday, September 11– 25 years on from 9/11, the international press reflects on the war on terror, its legacy and its failings. In France, the far-right National Rally party tries desperately to distance itself from the overtly racist comments of one of its security officials, made while on duty for his day job as a police officer. Finally, a fossilised feather may give us new insights into why birds survived the asteroid that killed the dinosaurs.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Italy's Emma Bonino, champion of battles to legalise abortion and divorce, dies at 78</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b971e17a4ea6be702cfb84ac18e92991e758104a5e7a6febe5df9302d75c90b</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:33:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-italy-s-emma-bonino-champion-of-battles-to-legalise-abortion-and-divorce-dies-at-78--08dac3031ddb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-italy-s-emma-bonino-champion-of-battles-to-legalise-abortion-and-divorce-dies-at-78" /><summary type="html">Veteran feminist activist Emma Bonino, who rose to political prominence in the 1970s as a leader of campaigns to legalise abortion and divorce in heavily Roman Catholic Italy over the objections of the Vatican, has died aged 78. Bonino, who was diagnosed with lung cancer in 2015, served as foreign minister and European commissioner but failed in her bid to become Italy's first woman president.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Space: Europe urged to find its path</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:324f88130f0700fb3f2f8483ac06dd4ce28e20ba5b2c7c1ad8cbe10f82098f14</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T21:03:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/space-europe-urged-to-find-its-path-from-crewed-spaceflight-to-communications--25ea30849574.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/space-europe-urged-to-find-its-path-from-crewed-spaceflight-to-communications" /><summary type="html">From communications to crewed spaceflight, French President Emmanuel Macron and European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen called for Europeans to "act" on a massive scale to find their place in the space race on Thursday – notably, against the United States and China. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Svetla Ben-Itzhak, Assistant Professor of Space and International Relations and Deputy Director of the West Space Scholars Programme at Johns Hopkins University, explains that "Europe does have world-class scientific and industrial capabilities, as well as aspirations, but it lacks the investment, the launch cadence, the scale as well as the degree of political integration that the US and China possess".</summary></entry><entry><title>'No facts': Morocco denies involvement in deadly Ceuta migrant rush</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:099e45b9a4c448b5730caf2e2aa166d45a5ee5c3ad0db87b6568267f561a88e9</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:32:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-no-facts-morocco-denies-involvement-in-deadly-ceuta-migrant-rush--ae85c7241bed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-no-facts-morocco-denies-involvement-in-deadly-ceuta-migrant-rush" /><summary type="html">Moroccan authorities said on Thursday there were "no facts" establishing its involvement in the migrant rush into Spain's North African exclave of Ceuta in July. It was the kingdom's first official response to a Spanish police report accusing its security forces of "total permissiveness" when the mass crossing took place.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>International Space Summit: Europe plays catch-up with US and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:684ec64e4f87b848d1e0ffbdbdbcb947269a73efd4784bda9c782a94fcaa4e55</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T15:28:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20260910-international-space-summit-europe-plays-catch-up-with-us-and-china--975a45d2435a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20260910-international-space-summit-europe-plays-catch-up-with-us-and-china" /><summary type="html">The space sector is booming. The global industry expected to reach a value of €2 trillion mark by 2040. But behind this spectacular growth lies major geopolitical challenges, particularly for Europe. In this edition, FRANCE 24’s Charles Pellegrin speaks to Kai-Uwe Schrogl at the International Space Summit in Paris. Schrogl, a political affairs adviser to the European Space Agency, answers questions about the future of the great beyond and Europe’s place in the new space race.</summary><category term="People &amp; Profit" /></entry></feed>
